Since the cones are similar, the ratio of their radii equals the ratio of their heights:  
\[
\frac{\text{Radius of small cone}}{\text{Radius of large cone}} = \frac{\text{Height of small cone}}{\text{Height of large cone}}
\]  
Substituting the known radii and heights:  
\[
\frac{r}{R} = \frac{x}{x + 24}
\]  


